From e206d84f13de1c27f016e96c385db9f5364b584d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: pair-spec lane <pair-spec@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 05:21:22 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(uniswap-v2): pair negative controls by execution

Run swap on the exact bytes in EthLib among two token accounts and on
the checked source in the matching world, then on swap without its
reserve update (solar's compile of the mutant source and SolidCore's
translation of it), the bytes with a jump target moved, a mismatched
world and a closed world. The runs are evaluated (#guard): EthLib's
processMessage is well-founded recursion the kernel does not reduce.
Each refusal is a kernel theorem over every observable with the
executed features: the published spec refuses the mutant's reserves,
the wrong-K spec refuses the pair's, the published clause accepts them.

Replace the pair statement's premise NestedSlotsSeparated, which is
unsatisfiable, with HashScope: the keccak words the spec reads
(balanceOf[0], allowance[0][s]) avoid the pair's 13 fixed slots.
